# 🔐 O-Saft – OWASP SSL Advanced Forensic Tool

## 📌 Objective
To evaluate SSL/TLS configurations of a target web server using **O-Saft**, understand the cipher suites, hashing algorithms, certificate info, and detect possible vulnerabilities in the SSL implementation.

---

## 🧰 Tool Used
**O-Saft** (OWASP SSL Advanced Forensic Tool)  
Language: Perl  
Platform: Linux/Windows  
Official: [https://owasp.org/www-project-o-saft/](https://owasp.org/www-project-o-saft/)

## 🧪 Tasks Performed

### 1️⃣ Basic Info: List SSL Certificate Details

```bash
./o-saft -h <target-domain>

2️⃣ Check Supported Cipher Suites
./o-saft -h <target-domain> +cipher
✅ Lists all supported ciphers by the server.

Example Output:

TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256
TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA
...
You can also test specific ciphers:

./o-saft -h <target-domain> --cipher=TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA
3️⃣ View SSL/TLS Versions Supported
./o-saft -h <target-domain> +version
✅ Shows whether SSLv2, SSLv3, TLS 1.0/1.1/1.2/1.3 are supported.

4️⃣ List Archive File (General Linux Skill)
tar -tvf archive.tar.gz
✅ Used to list contents of an archive without extracting (relevant in forensic review when analyzing dumped configs).



